LEGALTECH FIRESTORE SETUP

1) Collections Created
- users
- contractAnalyses
- advocates
- reservations
- chatHistory

2) Files
- DATABASE.json: detailed schema and examples
- DATABASE.js: firebase connection + create helpers + seedDemoData()

3) Firebase Link Steps
- Create Firebase project in console
- Enable Firestore Database (Production or Test mode)
- Enable Authentication > Email/Password
- Copy Firebase web config and place in .env.local:
  NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=...
  NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=...
  NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=...
  NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=...
  NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=...
  NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=...

4) Install SDK
- npm i firebase

5) Use In App
- Import db/helpers from DATABASE.js
- Call createUser/createContractAnalysis/createAdvocate/createReservation/createChatHistory

6) Optional Seed
- Call seedDemoData() once from a script/page after env vars are valid

7) Firestore Rules Starter (replace with strict production rules)
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
    }

    match /contractAnalyses/{analysisId} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null &&
        request.auth.uid == resource.data.userId;
      allow create: if request.auth != null &&
        request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.userId;
    }

    match /advocates/{advocateId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if request.auth != null;
    }

    match /reservations/{reservationId} {
      allow create: if request.auth != null &&
        request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.clientId;
      allow read: if request.auth != null &&
        (request.auth.uid == resource.data.clientId ||
         request.auth.uid == resource.data.advocateId);
      allow update: if request.auth != null &&
        (request.auth.uid == resource.data.clientId ||
         request.auth.uid == resource.data.advocateId);
    }

    match /chatHistory/{chatId} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null &&
        request.auth.uid in resource.data.participants;
      allow create: if request.auth != null &&
        request.auth.uid in request.resource.data.participants;
    }
  }
}

Note:
- If advocates collection uses separate IDs (not auth uid), map advocate auth uid in user profile
  and use that uid in reservations/chat access checks.
